{
  "_comment": "The ownership map: which first-party module owns which file, as globs over TREE PATHS (paths relative to the package root: server/ or agent-hub/ for the core, modules/<id>/<moduleDir>/ for a module; web client tree paths start with src/). Rules and CLI in scripts/module-map.mjs: `core` exceptions win over module globs; a `!glob` takes files out of that module's own globs; a file may match ONE module only; a file that matches nothing is core; a colocated test, testkit, golden, fixture or .d.ts follows its source unless a glob names it, and in the web client so do x.types.ts, x.helpers.ts, x.constants.ts and x(.module).css. The web client's i18n chunks src/i18n/en/<ns>.generated.mjs have the owner of the server namespace of the same name. Check with `node scripts/module-map.mjs --check`; measure with `--summary --pkg agent-hub`.",
